BT /F1 12 Tf 50 750 Td 14 TL (Computer Networking Guide: Architecture and Protocols.) Tj T* (Chapter 1: The OSI Reference Model.) Tj T* (The Open Systems Interconnection model defines seven architectural layers:) Tj T* (Layer 1 Physical Layer transmits raw bit streams over cables and radio frequencies.) Tj T* (Layer 2 Data Link Layer uses MAC hardware addresses to transfer frames across switches.) Tj T* (Layer 3 Network Layer is responsible for logical IP packet routing across routers.) Tj T* (Layer 4 Transport Layer provides host-to-host communication using TCP or UDP protocols.) Tj T* (Layer 5 Session Layer manages dialogues and connection sessions.) Tj T* (Layer 6 Presentation Layer handles syntax translation and SSL/TLS data encryption.) Tj T* (Layer 7 Application Layer supports end-user protocols including HTTP, DNS, and SMTP.) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
8 0 obj
<< /Length 545 >>
stream
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 750 Td 14 TL (Chapter 2: The Domain Name System \(DNS\).) Tj T* (DNS translates alphanumeric domain names into numeric IP addresses.) Tj T* (DNS servers primarily listen on UDP port 53 for low-overhead query resolution.) Tj T* (However, when DNS responses exceed 512 bytes, DNS automatically falls back to TCP port 53.) Tj T* (Recursive resolvers query root name servers, Top-Level Domain \(TLD\) servers, and authoritative servers.) Tj T* (DNS caching reduces query latency across local networks and operating systems.) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 687 >>
stream
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 750 Td 14 TL (Chapter 3: Transmission Control Protocol \(TCP\) and UDP.) Tj T* (TCP provides reliable, ordered, and error-checked delivery of a stream of bytes.) Tj T* (To establish a connection, TCP performs a three-way handshake:) Tj T* (Step 1: The client sends a SYN \(synchronize\) packet to the server.) Tj T* (Step 2: The server responds with a SYN-ACK \(synchronize-acknowledge\) packet.) Tj T* (Step 3: The client replies with an ACK \(acknowledge\) packet.) Tj T* (TCP uses sequence numbers and sliding window flow control to prevent buffer overflows.) Tj T* (Conversely, UDP is a connectionless datagram protocol without handshakes or retransmission.) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
